/-!
# Signal Double Ratchet: Extraction to Security

Instantiates the hax-extracted `DoubleratchetDeps` of the crate `doubleratchet-hax`
(<https://github.com/spitters/signal-hax>) with libcrux-specs primitives and an X25519 function
`sm` (`doubleratchetDepsOf sm`), and carries the game of the extracted session to the Signal
double ratchet of `Signal.DoubleRatchet_UC`. The instance `defaultDoubleratchetDeps` takes the
libcrux `x25519_scalarmult`, and `specDoubleratchetDeps` the RFC 7748 specification
`Spec.x25519_spec`.

```
doubleratchet-hax                        (Rust: the typestate session, generic in the
        |  haxpipeT --emit-certified       trait DoubleRatchetDeps)
Doubleratchet_haxpipe                    (DoubleratchetDeps: hmac_sha256, hkdf_extract,
        |                                  hkdf_expand, x25519, aead_encrypt, aead_decrypt)
        |  doubleratchetDepsOf sm          (libcrux-specs HMAC-SHA256, HKDF-SHA256, X25519 sm)
        |  drHomOf                         (vecToArrayInt carries them to the model)
ExtractedCorrespondence                  (sm_extracted over Session_* = encoded sm_real)
        |  signalDR_extracted_advantage_le
Signal.DoubleRatchet_UC                  (DH CKA, HKDF root step, FS-AEAD)
```

The extraction computes on byte arrays and the model on `Vector UInt8 32`. The instance
`defaultDoubleratchetDeps` decodes its arguments (`decodeKey`, the inverse of
`vecToArrayInt`), applies the libcrux-specs operation and encodes the result: `hmac_sha256` is
`hmac_sha256_32`, `hkdf_extract` and `hkdf_expand` are `hkdf_extract_32` and `hkdf_expand_32`,
and `x25519` is `sm`. Encryption is XOR: `aead_encrypt` and `aead_decrypt` are
`xorBytes`, the XOR of the decoded 32-byte key and the first 32 entries of the text (`wxorEnc`
on words). The trait's `aead_encrypt` takes texts of up to `MAX_PLAINTEXT_LEN = 256` bytes;
`xorBytes` reads 32 of them, and the theorems here use it at the 32-byte encodings
`vecToArrayInt` of words only.

The Diffie–Hellman CKA of the model is over the prime-order subgroup `G25519 B` of Curve25519
generated by a point `B` of order `ℓ`, with exponents `ZMod ℓ` and elements encoded by their
u-coordinate `encU`. The hypothesis is `X25519HomOf sm bp B`, the RFC 7748 correctness of `sm`
on that subgroup. At the libcrux X25519 it is `X25519Hom B` (a `Fact` for the instances of the UC
statement); at the specification `Spec.x25519_spec` and the base point `B9` it is the theorem
`X25519HomOf.spec_B9`. The extraction computes X25519 with a
32-byte key `sk`, which RFC 7748 clamps; the clamped scalars `clampE sk` reach at most `2^251`
residues modulo `ℓ`, so the model draws the secret key `(sk, b)` of `Sk = Vector UInt8 32 × Bool`
with the exponent `signedE (sk, b) = ± clampE sk`. The extraction sees the bytes of `sk` only,
and `encU` identifies `T` and `-T`, so the sign changes no encoded value; the law `signedClamp`
of the signed clamped scalar is within `Δ25519 ≤ 2^-126` of uniform on `ZMod ℓ`
(`signedClampCert`), and each of the `msgs.length + 1` exponent draws of the CKA is charged
`Δ25519`.

`signalDR_e2e_uc_secure`: the game of the extracted session at `defaultDoubleratchetDeps`
UC-emulates the encoded ideal game, through the class route (`PureGame`, `GameAdvBoundC`,
`UCFromGameC.uc`); the bound for adversary `A` and environment `Z` is `signalDRBound` at
`envReduction A Z` precomposed with the encoding of the views (`encodedRed`): the DDH advantages
in `G25519 B`, the PRG advantages of the HKDF root step and the FS-AEAD advantages of the
libcrux symmetric ratchet against explicit reductions, summed over the epochs, plus
`(msgs.length + 1) * Δ25519`.

`signalDR_extracted_corrupt_advantage_le` and `signalDR_extracted_adaptive_advantage_le`: the
session functions of the crate at `defaultDoubleratchetDeps`, as the secure-messaging scheme
`signalDRLibcruxSM B` of `ExtractedScheme` (`Uninitialized_establish` opens the initiator's
first epoch, the halves of `Session_dh_ratchet` open the other epochs and receive them), in the
ACD corruption game with forward secrecy and post-compromise security and in the game with an
adaptive challenge epoch. Under `X25519Hom B` the scheme simulates the ACD construction over the
Diffie–Hellman CKA `dhCKAOf (G25519 B) signedE`, whose secret keys are the libcrux keys
`(sk, b)`; the bound is that of `sm_corrupt_advantage_le` (`sm_adaptive_corrupt_advantage_le`)
at explicit reductions of the encoded adversary. A corruption reveals the bytes of the secret
key, which the exponent `signedE (sk, b)` does not determine. In the corruption game with
`2 ≤ ΔFS`, `2 ≤ ΔPCS` the CKA terms are DDH advantages in `G25519 B` of the reductions
`ckaCorruptDDHRedOf signedE ΔFS ΔPCS`, each plus `4 Δ25519` for the two exponent draws of the
epochs `t* - 1` and `t*` in the real and in the ideal game (`dhCKAOf_corrupt_advantage_le` at
`signedClampCert`). In the adaptive game, for an adversary of at most `q` queries and with
`2 ≤ ΔFS`, `2 ≤ ΔPCS`, the bound is the sum over the epochs `e ≤ q` of the same terms at the
guessing reductions of the epochs, the CKA terms DDH advantages in `G25519 B` of
`ckaCorruptDDHRedOf signedE ΔFS ΔPCS`, plus `(q + 1) * 8 * Δ25519`.
`signalDR_extracted_adaptive_advantage_le_tsum` (with `2 ≤ ΔFS`, `1 ≤ ΔPCS`) is the bound summed
over all epochs, with the CKA corruption advantages of `dhCKAOf (G25519 B) signedE`. The two
bounds hold for the scheme `signalDRSMOf B sm` of every X25519 function `sm` with
`X25519HomOf sm bp B` (`signalDR_extracted_corrupt_advantage_le_of_hom`,
`signalDR_extracted_adaptive_advantage_le_of_hom`); the libcrux statements are their instances.

`signalDR_spec_corrupt_advantage_le` and `signalDR_spec_adaptive_advantage_le`: the same bounds
for `signalDRSpecSM B9`, the session functions at `specDoubleratchetDeps` with the CKA over
`G25519 B9`. The correctness of `Spec.x25519_spec` on the subgroup is a theorem, so these
statements have no X25519 hypothesis; an implementation of X25519 equal to `Spec.x25519_spec`
gives the session functions of `specDoubleratchetDeps`.

## References

* J. Alwen, S. Coretti, Y. Dodis, "The Double Ratchet: Security Notions, Proofs, and
  Modularization for the Signal Protocol", Eurocrypt 2019: the secure-messaging game and its
  decomposition into CKA, PRF-PRNG and FS-AEAD.
* R. Canetti, P. Jain, M. Swanberg, M. Varia, "Universally Composable End-to-End Secure
  Messaging", CRYPTO 2022 (ePrint 2022/376). The UC statement here is the lift of the
  secure-messaging game through `UCFromGameC`, not the functionality of that paper.
* T. Perrin, M. Marlinspike, "The Double Ratchet Algorithm", Signal specification, 2016.
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace CatCrypt.Crypto.Signal.DoubleRatchet.SurfaceDeps

open CatCrypt.Core CatCrypt.Prob CatCrypt.Crypto
open CatCrypt.Examples.SymmRatchet
open CatCrypt.Crypto.Messaging CatCrypt.Crypto.Signal.DoubleRatchet_CKA
open CatCrypt.Crypto.Signal.DoubleRatchet_UC
open CatCryptCore.Examples.CyclicGroupDDH
open CatCrypt.Crypto.UCDSL
open CatCrypt.Crypto.Libcrux.ConcreteInstances
open CatCrypt.Crypto.Libcrux.Extraction.Libcrux_specs
open CatCrypt.Hax.ReprBridge
open CatCrypt.Crypto.ECC CatCrypt.Crypto.Libcrux.Bridge_X25519Group
open scoped ENNReal

/-- The ghost record of the typestate FSM (the trait `DoubleRatchetGhost` of the crate's module
`typestate_fsm`): the ghost state is the ordered trace of actions, and each hook appends
`kind`, its leading argument, the payload length and the payload, with `kind` `0` for
`send step msg_key`, `1` for `recv step msg_key` and `2` for `event tag step` (payload
`#[step]`). -/
def doubleratchetGhostRecord (kind : Int) (ghost : Array Int) (tag : Int)
    (payload : Array Int) : Array Int :=
  ghost ++ #[kind, tag, payload.size] ++ payload

/-- A byte array read as a 32-byte key: entry `i` truncated to a byte, `0` past the end. The
decoding is total and inverts `vecToArrayInt` (`decodeKey_vecToArrayInt`). -/
def decodeKey (a : Array Int) : Vector UInt8 32 :=
  Vector.ofFn fun i => (a.getD i 0).toNat.toUInt8

/-- `decodeKey` is a left inverse of `vecToArrayInt`: decoding the encoding of a 32-byte vector
returns the vector. -/
theorem decodeKey_vecToArrayInt (v : Vector UInt8 32) : decodeKey (vecToArrayInt v) = v := by
  ext i hi
  simp [decodeKey, vecToArrayInt]

/-! ## The libcrux primitives of the double ratchet

The chain step is HMAC-SHA256 of the chain key on a constant block (`ckConst`), as in the
crate (`kdf_ck ck 2` the message key, `kdf_ck ck 1` the next chain key); the root step is
HKDF-SHA256 with the root key as salt and the Diffie–Hellman output as input keying material,
expanded under two info blocks into the next root key and the chain key. The libcrux
primitives are opaque; the protocol composition is transparent. -/

/-- The HMAC message block of the chain-step constant `c`: 32 bytes `c`. -/
def ckConst (c : UInt8) : Vector UInt8 32 := Vector.replicate 32 c

/-- The block `Hax.repeat_ 1 32` of the extraction decodes to `ckConst 1`. -/
theorem decodeKey_repeat_one : decodeKey (Hax.repeat_ 1 32) = ckConst 1 := by
  decide

/-- The block `Hax.repeat_ 2 32` of the extraction decodes to `ckConst 2`. -/
theorem decodeKey_repeat_two : decodeKey (Hax.repeat_ 2 32) = ckConst 2 := by
  decide

/-- Libcrux-backed chain step: the message key `HMAC(ck, ckConst 2)` and the next chain key
`HMAC(ck, ckConst 1)`. -/
noncomputable def libcrux_prg : PRGDef (Vector UInt8 32) where
  stretch := fun ck => (hmac_sha256_32 ck (ckConst 2), hmac_sha256_32 ck (ckConst 1))

/-- The libcrux-backed symmetric ratchet: the chain step `libcrux_prg` and XOR encryption under
the message key. -/
noncomputable def libcrux_fsaeadConfig :
    Signal.FSAEAD.FSAEADConfig (Vector UInt8 32) :=
  ⟨libcrux_prg, wxorEnc⟩

/-- The HKDF info block of the next root key. -/
def rootInfoRk : Vector UInt8 32 := Vector.replicate 32 1

/-- The HKDF info block of the chain key of the root step. -/
def rootInfoCk : Vector UInt8 32 := Vector.replicate 32 2

/-- The libcrux root step on bytes: `HKDF-Extract(rk, dh)` expanded under `rootInfoRk` and
`rootInfoCk`. -/
noncomputable def libcruxKdfRk (rk dh : Vector UInt8 32) : Vector UInt8 32 × Vector UInt8 32 :=
  (hkdf_expand_32 (hkdf_extract_32 rk dh) rootInfoRk,
    hkdf_expand_32 (hkdf_extract_32 rk dh) rootInfoCk)

/-- The libcrux root step of the model: `libcruxKdfRk` at the encoding `encG` of the
Diffie–Hellman output. -/
noncomputable def libcruxRootKdf {G : Type} (encG : G → Vector UInt8 32) (rk : Vector UInt8 32)
    (I : G) : Vector UInt8 32 × Vector UInt8 32 :=
  libcruxKdfRk rk (encG I)

/-- The XOR of the decoded 32-byte key and the first 32 entries of the text, encoded back as a
32-entry array: the encryption and decryption of `defaultDoubleratchetDeps`. -/
noncomputable def xorBytes (k m : Array Int) : Array Int :=
  vecToArrayInt (CryptoWord.wxor (decodeKey k) (decodeKey m))

/-! ## Extraction instance -/

/-- The primitives of the extraction on byte arrays at the X25519 function `sm`:
`hmac_sha256_32`, `hkdf_extract_32`, `hkdf_expand_32` and `sm` of the decoded arguments, encoded
back by `vecToArrayInt`; `aead_encrypt` and `aead_decrypt` are `xorBytes` of the key and the
text, whatever the length and the associated data. The ghost hooks `send`, `recv`, `event`
append to the trace (`doubleratchetGhostRecord`). -/
@[reducible] noncomputable def doubleratchetDepsOf
    (sm : Vector UInt8 32 → Vector UInt8 32 → Vector UInt8 32) :
    Doubleratchet.DoubleratchetDeps where
  event ghost tag step := doubleratchetGhostRecord 2 ghost tag #[step]
  send := doubleratchetGhostRecord 0
  recv := doubleratchetGhostRecord 1
  hmac_sha256 k m := vecToArrayInt (hmac_sha256_32 (decodeKey k) (decodeKey m))
  hkdf_extract s i := vecToArrayInt (hkdf_extract_32 (decodeKey s) (decodeKey i))
  hkdf_expand p i := vecToArrayInt (hkdf_expand_32 (decodeKey p) (decodeKey i))
  x25519 sk pk := vecToArrayInt (sm (decodeKey sk) (decodeKey pk))
  aead_encrypt k m _ _ := xorBytes k m
  aead_decrypt k c _ _ := xorBytes k c

/-- The primitives of the extraction with the libcrux X25519: `doubleratchetDepsOf` at
`x25519_scalarmult`. -/
noncomputable instance defaultDoubleratchetDeps : Doubleratchet.DoubleratchetDeps :=
  doubleratchetDepsOf x25519_scalarmult

open CatCrypt.Crypto.KeyAgreement.X25519 in
/-- The primitives of the extraction with the X25519 function of the RFC 7748 specification:
`doubleratchetDepsOf` at `Spec.x25519_spec`. -/
@[reducible] noncomputable def specDoubleratchetDeps : Doubleratchet.DoubleratchetDeps :=
  doubleratchetDepsOf Spec.x25519_spec

/-- `vecToArrayInt` carries the primitives of `doubleratchetDepsOf sm` to those of the Signal
double ratchet over the subgroup `G25519 B` at the root step `libcruxRootKdf encU` and the
symmetric ratchet `libcrux_fsaeadConfig`, at the plaintext length `32`, under the RFC 7748
correctness `X25519HomOf sm bp B` of the X25519 function `sm`: a secret key `(sk, b)` is encoded
by the bytes of `sk` and has the exponent `signedE (sk, b)`, group elements are encoded by
`encU`. -/
theorem drHomOf {B : Curve25519Point} [Fact (addOrderOf B = curve25519SubgroupOrder)]
    {sm : Vector UInt8 32 → Vector UInt8 32 → Vector UInt8 32}
    {bp : Vector UInt8 32 → Vector UInt8 32} (hH : X25519HomOf sm bp B) :
    ExtractedCorrespondence.DrHom (inst := doubleratchetDepsOf sm) (G25519 B)
      (hkdfRoot (libcruxRootKdf encU))
      (Signal.FSAEAD.toPRG libcrux_fsaeadConfig) (Signal.FSAEAD.toAEAD libcrux_fsaeadConfig) 32
      vecToArrayInt (vecToArrayInt ∘ encU) (vecToArrayInt ∘ Prod.fst) signedE vecToArrayInt
      vecToArrayInt vecToArrayInt := by
  let _ : Doubleratchet.DoubleratchetDeps := doubleratchetDepsOf sm
  exact {
    dh_eq := fun s T => by
      simp only [Doubleratchet.x25519, Function.comp_apply, decodeKey_vecToArrayInt,
        hH.scalarmult_elemPow s.1 s.2 T]
    root_rk_eq := fun rk I => by
      simp only [Doubleratchet.hkdf_expand, Doubleratchet.hkdf_extract, decodeKey_vecToArrayInt,
        decodeKey_repeat_one, Function.comp_apply, hkdfRoot, libcruxRootKdf, libcruxKdfRk,
        rootInfoRk, ckConst]
    root_ck_eq := fun rk I => by
      simp only [Doubleratchet.hkdf_expand, Doubleratchet.hkdf_extract, decodeKey_vecToArrayInt,
        decodeKey_repeat_two, Function.comp_apply, hkdfRoot, libcruxRootKdf, libcruxKdfRk,
        rootInfoCk, ckConst]
    msg_key_eq := fun s => by
      simp only [Doubleratchet.hmac_sha256, Doubleratchet.ck_const, decodeKey_vecToArrayInt,
        decodeKey_repeat_two, Signal.FSAEAD.toPRG, libcrux_fsaeadConfig, libcrux_prg, PRGDef.core]
    chain_key_eq := fun s => by
      simp only [Doubleratchet.hmac_sha256, Doubleratchet.ck_const, decodeKey_vecToArrayInt,
        decodeKey_repeat_one, Signal.FSAEAD.toPRG, libcrux_fsaeadConfig, libcrux_prg, PRGDef.core]
    aead_eq := fun k m a => by
      simp only [Doubleratchet.aead_encrypt, xorBytes, decodeKey_vecToArrayInt,
        Signal.FSAEAD.toAEAD, libcrux_fsaeadConfig, EncDef.aead, wxorEnc] }

/-- `vecToArrayInt` carries the primitives of `defaultDoubleratchetDeps` to those of the Signal
double ratchet over the subgroup `G25519 B` at the root step `libcruxRootKdf encU` and the
symmetric ratchet `libcrux_fsaeadConfig`, at the plaintext length `32`, under the RFC 7748
correctness `X25519Hom B` of X25519: a secret key `(sk, b)` is encoded by the bytes of `sk` and
has the exponent `signedE (sk, b)`, group elements are encoded by `encU`. -/
theorem defaultDrHom {B : Curve25519Point} [Fact (addOrderOf B = curve25519SubgroupOrder)]
    (hH : X25519Hom B) :
    ExtractedCorrespondence.DrHom (G25519 B) (hkdfRoot (libcruxRootKdf encU))
      (Signal.FSAEAD.toPRG libcrux_fsaeadConfig) (Signal.FSAEAD.toAEAD libcrux_fsaeadConfig) 32
      vecToArrayInt (vecToArrayInt ∘ encU) (vecToArrayInt ∘ Prod.fst) signedE vecToArrayInt
      vecToArrayInt vecToArrayInt :=
  drHomOf hH

/-! ## Security of the extracted double ratchet -/

section UC

open ExtractedCorrespondence UCConcrete

variable (B : Curve25519Point) [Fact (addOrderOf B = curve25519SubgroupOrder)]

/-- The Signal double ratchet game of the extracted session at `defaultDoubleratchetDeps`:
`Uninitialized_establish`, `Session_send`, `Session_dh_ratchet` and `Session_receive` on the
libcrux primitives, the plaintext length `32`, the Diffie–Hellman CKA over `G25519 B` with
elements encoded by `vecToArrayInt ∘ encU`, and secret keys `(sk, b)` drawn uniformly, encoded
by the bytes of `sk` and with the exponent `signedE (sk, b)`. -/
noncomputable abbrev signalDRLibcrux (msgs : List (List (Vector UInt8 32))) :
    Unit → SPComp (SMView (Array Int) (Array Int)) :=
  signalDRExtracted (Vector UInt8 32) (G25519 B) 32 vecToArrayInt (vecToArrayInt ∘ encU)
    (vecToArrayInt ∘ Prod.fst) signedE vecToArrayInt msgs

/-- The encoded ideal game of `signalDRLibcrux`. -/
noncomputable abbrev signalDRLibcruxIdeal (msgs : List (List (Vector UInt8 32))) :
    Unit → SPComp (SMView (Array Int) (Array Int)) :=
  signalDRIdealEnc (G25519 B) (vecToArrayInt ∘ encU) vecToArrayInt msgs

/-- The game of the extracted session does not touch the heap. -/
instance signalDRLibcrux_pureGame (msgs : List (List (Vector UInt8 32))) :
    PureGame (signalDRLibcrux B msgs) :=
  ⟨fun _ => SPComp.bind_isPure (SPComp.sample_isPure _) fun _ =>
    SPComp.bind_isPure (SPComp.sample_isPure _) fun _ =>
      SPComp.bind_isPure (SPComp.sample_isPure _) fun _ => SPComp.pure_isPure _⟩

/-- The encoded ideal game does not touch the heap. -/
instance signalDRLibcruxIdeal_pureGame (msgs : List (List (Vector UInt8 32))) :
    PureGame (signalDRLibcruxIdeal B msgs) :=
  ⟨fun _ => SPComp.bind_isPure (PureGame.isPure (G := signalDRIdeal (W := Vector UInt8 32)
    (G25519 B) msgs) ()) fun _ => SPComp.pure_isPure _⟩

variable [hH : Fact (X25519Hom B)]

/-- The per-adversary bound of the game of the extracted session: `signalDRBound` over
`G25519 B` at the root step `libcruxRootKdf encU` and the symmetric ratchet
`libcrux_fsaeadConfig`, at the distinguisher `encodedRed (encView _ _) A` of the views, plus
`Δ25519` for each of the `msgs.length + 1` exponent draws. -/
instance signalDRLibcrux_gameAdvBound (msgs : List (List (Vector UInt8 32))) :
    GameAdvBoundC (signalDRLibcrux B msgs) (signalDRLibcruxIdeal B msgs)
      (fun _ A => signalDRBound (G25519 B) (libcruxRootKdf encU) libcrux_fsaeadConfig msgs
        (encodedRed (encView (vecToArrayInt ∘ encU) vecToArrayInt) A) +
          (msgs.length + 1) * Δ25519) :=
  ⟨fun _ A => signalDR_extracted_advantage_le (defaultDrHom hH.out) signedClampCert rfl rfl
    msgs A⟩

/-- **UC security of the extracted Signal double ratchet.** The secure-messaging game of one
session of `doubleratchet-hax` (`Uninitialized_establish`, `Session_send`, `Session_dh_ratchet`,
`Session_receive`) at `defaultDoubleratchetDeps` (libcrux HMAC-SHA256, HKDF-SHA256 and
X25519, XOR encryption), with the Diffie–Hellman CKA over the subgroup `G25519 B` of a point
`B` of order `ℓ` under the RFC 7748 correctness `X25519Hom B` of X25519, UC-emulates the
encoded ideal game; the bound for the adversary `A` and the environment `Z` is `signalDRBound`
over `G25519 B` at the distinguisher `envReduction A Z` precomposed with the encoding of the
views, plus `(msgs.length + 1) * Δ25519` for the distance of the signed clamped scalars to
uniform exponents. -/
theorem signalDR_e2e_uc_secure (msgs : List (List (Vector UInt8 32))) (V : Type) :
    UCConcrete.UCEmulatesCSim (UCSpec.ofGame Unit (SMView (Array Int) (Array Int)) V)
      (UCProtocol.ofGame (signalDRLibcrux B msgs))
      (UCProtocol.ofGame (signalDRLibcruxIdeal B msgs)) id
      (UCConcrete.gameUCBound fun _ A => signalDRBound (G25519 B) (libcruxRootKdf encU)
        libcrux_fsaeadConfig msgs (encodedRed (encView (vecToArrayInt ∘ encU) vecToArrayInt) A) +
          (msgs.length + 1) * Δ25519) :=
  UCFromGameC.uc

end UC

/-! ## Forward secrecy and post-compromise security of the extracted double ratchet -/

section Corrupt

open ExtractedCorrespondence ExtractedScheme

variable (B : Curve25519Point) [Fact (addOrderOf B = curve25519SubgroupOrder)]

/-- The extracted double ratchet at `doubleratchetDepsOf sm` as a secure-messaging scheme:
`drExtractedSM` with the plaintext length `32`, root keys, chain keys, words and ciphertexts
encoded by `vecToArrayInt`, group elements of `G25519 B` by `vecToArrayInt ∘ encU`, and secret
keys `(sk, b)` drawn uniformly, encoded by the bytes of `sk` and with the exponent
`signedE (sk, b)`. -/
noncomputable abbrev signalDRSMOf (sm : Vector UInt8 32 → Vector UInt8 32 → Vector UInt8 32) :
    SMScheme Doubleratchet.Session_T (Array Int) (Vector UInt8 32 × Bool) (Vector UInt8 32)
      (Array Int) DrLeak :=
  drExtractedSM (inst := doubleratchetDepsOf sm) (Vector UInt8 32) (G := G25519 B)
    (Ct := Vector UInt8 32) 32 vecToArrayInt (vecToArrayInt ∘ encU) (vecToArrayInt ∘ Prod.fst)
    signedE vecToArrayInt vecToArrayInt

/-- The extracted double ratchet at `defaultDoubleratchetDeps` as a secure-messaging scheme:
`signalDRSMOf` at the libcrux X25519. -/
noncomputable abbrev signalDRLibcruxSM :
    SMScheme Doubleratchet.Session_T (Array Int) (Vector UInt8 32 × Bool) (Vector UInt8 32)
      (Array Int) DrLeak :=
  signalDRSMOf B x25519_scalarmult

open CatCrypt.Crypto.KeyAgreement.X25519 in
/-- The extracted double ratchet at `specDoubleratchetDeps` as a secure-messaging scheme:
`signalDRSMOf` at the X25519 function `Spec.x25519_spec` of the RFC 7748 specification. -/
noncomputable abbrev signalDRSpecSM :
    SMScheme Doubleratchet.Session_T (Array Int) (Vector UInt8 32 × Bool) (Vector UInt8 32)
      (Array Int) DrLeak :=
  signalDRSMOf B Spec.x25519_spec

/-- The encoding of the corruption answers of the ACD construction at the libcrux encodings. -/
noncomputable abbrev signalDRLibcruxLeak :
    SMPartySt (G25519 B × (Vector UInt8 32 × Bool)) (Vector UInt8 32) (Vector UInt8 32) →
      DrLeak :=
  drEncLeak vecToArrayInt (vecToArrayInt ∘ encU) (vecToArrayInt ∘ Prod.fst) signedE
    vecToArrayInt

/-- **Forward secrecy and post-compromise security of the extracted Signal double ratchet at an
X25519 function.** For the session functions of `doubleratchet-hax` at `doubleratchetDepsOf sm`
(libcrux HMAC-SHA256 and HKDF-SHA256, the X25519 function `sm`, XOR encryption), under the
RFC 7748 correctness `X25519HomOf sm bp B` of `sm` on the subgroup `G25519 B`, and with
`2 ≤ ΔFS`, `2 ≤ ΔPCS`, the advantage of every adversary `A` in the corruption game over
`signalDRSMOf B sm` is at most

* the DDH advantages in `G25519 B` of the reductions `ckaCorruptDDHRedOf signedE ΔFS ΔPCS` at
